course: dictionary
lesson: 9859
title: Signs that something is wrong
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A symptom is a sign that something is wrong, most often that a person is ill. You can feel a symptom, or someone else can notice it. «UK advice now is that children with mild symptoms can go to school if they have no fever and feel well enough.» Here symptoms are the signs of being unwell, such as a fever or a cough.
explain: Symptom also has a wider meaning: a sign that a problem exists. Litter is a symptom of a careless town. When you see rubbish everywhere, it shows that people are not looking after the place. Ask yourself: what is the sign, and what might it show?
explain: Look at the words around symptom. Fever, cough, rest and sore throat all point to illness, so the clues show that symptom is about being ill. Try your meaning in the sentence: if "a sign of illness" fits, you have it.
fact: A symptom is a sign of an illness that a person feels or notices.
fact: Examples of symptoms are a fever, a cough, a rash and a headache.
fact: The plural of symptom is symptoms.
fact: A symptom can also be a sign that a bad thing exists, like litter showing a careless town.
fact: Doctors use symptoms to help them find out what illness someone has.
exercise: «UK advice now is that children with mild symptoms can go to school if they have no fever and feel well enough.» What does symptoms mean here? | Lessons and homework | *Signs of an illness, such as a cough or a runny nose | Rules about school dinners | Places where children play
exercise: Return to sport goes in stages, «dropping back a stage if symptoms return.» What should you do if symptoms come back? | Skip the rest of the week's training | Start with a full match straight away | *Go back a stage and take it more gently | Keep going at the same speed
exercise: «Litter is a symptom of a careless town.» What does symptom mean here? | *A sign that a problem exists | A type of illness | A kind of rubbish bin | A town with lots of parks
test: «High blood pressure has no symptoms but strains the heart over years.» What does has no symptoms mean? | It is cured by a good night's sleep | *It gives no obvious signs that a person can feel or notice | It is very painful and sudden | It always comes with a headache
test: Which word is the plural of symptom? | symptomy | symptomes | *symptoms
exam: Which of these is a symptom of a cold? | *A runny nose | A library book | A blue sky | A bicycle
